# Onto scheduled jobs — install with `crontab -e` as the `io` user.
#
# No long-lived scheduler process: the target is a Pi already running several
# services, and a scheduler thread would sit in memory all day for jobs that
# run once an hour. cron costs nothing when idle.
#
# Every job is idempotent and due-gated: cron fires dumbly, the command itself
# decides what is actually due. A missed run is caught up on the next tick and
# a doubled run changes nothing.

ONTO=/home/io/onto/backend
FLASK=/home/io/onto/backend/.venv/bin/flask

# Nightly tidy: prune rate-limit counters and other unbounded tables.
17 3 * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK housekeeping >> /home/io/onto/logs/housekeeping.log 2>&1

# Nightly backup. SQLite's online backup is safe against a live WAL database —
# a plain `cp` of a file being written is not.
30 3 * * * /home/io/onto/deploy/backup.sh >> /home/io/onto/logs/backup.log 2>&1

# Materialise recurring goals into each user's new week/month. Hourly and
# dumb on purpose: the command checks each user's own timezone and does
# nothing unless their week or month actually turned over.
5 * * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK rollover >> /home/io/onto/logs/rollover.log 2>&1

# Pull fresh events into the shared corpus from every enabled source.
# City-wide, never per-user (one corpus for everyone). Re-runs update
# rather than duplicate.
15 */6 * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK ingest >> /home/io/onto/logs/ingest.log 2>&1

# Expire past events and re-check the stalest source URLs, so nothing is
# ever suggested from a dead link or the past.
45 2 * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK verify-events >> /home/io/onto/logs/verify.log 2>&1

# Tier-3 LLM research through SearXNG. Twice a week at a quiet hour: it
# costs free-tier LLM calls and its yield is validated hard (URL must
# answer 200, date must be future) before anything enters the corpus.
20 5 * * 2,5 cd $ONTO && $FLASK research >> /home/io/onto/logs/research.log 2>&1

# Match corpus events to people's discovery-enabled goals. Nightly; the
# per-user weekly suggestion cap keeps the app quiet by default.
40 5 * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK match >> /home/io/onto/logs/match.log 2>&1

# The weekly/daily notes. Hourly and dumb: the command decides who is due
# from each user's frequency, hour, and timezone, and last_sent_on stops
# double-sends. Email dry-run config makes this safe on a first deploy.
0 * * * * cd $ONTO && $FLASK send-digests >> /home/io/onto/logs/digests.log 2>&1

# Repair the LLM model chain if it has rotted. The free catalogue churns
# without notice; a chain that worked last week can be entirely dead this
# week, taking research and digests down with it. This only rebuilds a
# chain that stopped working — it will NOT reorder a working chain to chase
# a faster model. Choosing on quality stays a human decision, from
# /admin/models. Twice a week; costs a few free-tier calls when healthy.
35 4 * * 1,4 cd $ONTO && $FLASK refresh-chain >> /home/io/onto/logs/chain.log 2>&1
